ource name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINRIKI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KENJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINRIKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINRIKI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINRIKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A reactor (101) is set at a low vacuum of 0.1 Torr.  A butyl acetate solution, in which Pb(DPM)2 is dissolved at 0.1 mol/l, is transported from a Pb material source (105) to a vaporizer (105b) through flow control means (105a) that controls the flow rate of the material.  The vaporizer (105b) vaporizes the butyl acetate and the Pb(DPM)2 dissolved in it.  The vaporized raw materials, together with helium gas at 250 sccm, are transported to a showerhead (103) so that the materials at their respective low partial pressures may reach a wafer (104) in the reactor (101).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un réacteur (101) défini à un faible niveau de vide de 0,1 Torr. Une solution d'acétate de butyle, dans laquelle le Pb(DPM)2 est dissous à 0,1 mol/l, est transportée depuis une source de matière Pb (105) vers un vaporisateur (105b) à travers des moyens de régulation de l'écoulement (105a) régulant la vitesse d'écoulement de la matière. Le vaporisateur (105b) vaporise l'acétate de butyle et le Pb(DPM)2 dissous dans l'acétate. Les matières premières vaporisées, ainsi que le gaz hélium à 250 sccm, sont transportés vers une pomme de douche (103) de manière que les matières à des pressions partielles basses puissent atteindre une plaquette (104) dans le réacteur (101).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>